//   section     : "blog", "news" or "value-for-money"
//   docx        : the .docx, relative to this Articles folder
//   imageFolder : web folder holding the article's pictures (the same pictures that are inside the .docx)
//   slug        : the URL, /blog/{slug}; leave out to use the image folder name
//   date        : publish date, yyyy-MM-dd; leave out to use the Word file's created date
//   cardImage   : optional smaller picture (file name inside imageFolder) for article cards
//   twoWheeler  : false for a car article (default true)
//   morePhotos  : false leaves out the "More photos" section of folder pictures not used in the Word file
//   draft       : true keeps the entry off the site
//   links       : internal links added to the text: { "text": words to link, "href": "/blog/...", "context": optional longer
//                 phrase holding the words, to choose which occurrence }. Only paragraph and list text is linked.
//   imageMap    : { "picture name inside the .docx (word/media)": "file in imageFolder" } for pictures whose folder copy is
//                 not the identical file (for example a watermarked version). Identical files are found without it.
// The Word file's Heading 1 becomes the H1, the first paragraph the intro and meta description, the first picture the
// cover, and the Word "Title" property (File > Info) the title shown in Google.
